--
-- PostGIS's lifecycle with commits in place, in a database of its own:
-- ALTER EXTENSION postgis UPDATE, with committed and uncommitted
-- versioned data on two branches, keeps every value and index, leaves
-- nothing new to commit and still enforces typmods; commits from before
-- and after it check out, reset, diff and merge.  (A PostGIS build has one
-- version, so the update goes to PostGIS's "ANY" version, which runs no
-- SQL, and back from it through the upgrade script every PostGIS release
-- ships, which replaces each of its functions, operators and operator
-- classes.)  DROP EXTENSION postgis is refused while versioned columns on
-- another branch use it, CASCADE or not.
--
\set ECHO none
c1|t
branch side|t
checkout side|t
side commit|t
checkout main|t
ERROR:  cannot drop extension postgis because objects on branch "side" depend on it
ERROR:  cannot drop extension postgis because objects on branch "side" depend on it
still installed|1
reset main|t
checkout side|t
side intact|t
checkout main|t
version|ANY
main values|t
main index|t
main status|public.gis_ext modified
commit at ANY|t
version again|t
main values|t
main index|t
main status|0
checkout side|t
side values|t
side index|t
side status|public.gis_side modified
side commit|t
ERROR:  Geometry type (Point) does not match column type (Polygon)
checkout main|t
merge side|{0,0,"merge successful"}
merged|t
merged index|t
diff c1..c2|20|modified
reset to c1|t
c1 values|t
c1 index|t
reset to c2|t
c2 values|t
branch at c1|t
checkout old|t
old values|t
old index|t
checkout main|t
